        "id": 66378,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-13T19:23:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jagarciao\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jagarciao/48/2010_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jagarciao:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Sounds like good times. I just got a group of friends to start playing dreadball… maybe I'll bring kaosball to the next league game day</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>They would be different enough I think to justify having both. KB is a much more streamlined, beer &amp; pretzles deal. Dreadball never struck me as being that way, though I have never played it. Just starting to find miniature games myself really since they have been inbreeding with boardgame sensibilities (which is much more my style).</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
