        "username": "jagarciao",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jagarciao/{size}/2010_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-13T20:20:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yeah, that's the vibe I got from it. Kaosball seems like more fun on the one-off games with lots of smack talk and a few beverages. Dreadball is really best in the league experience where you build your team through a season... it really appealed more to my friends who are actually into sports and stuff.</p><p>I, too, am very new at miniature games (and definitely picked up waaaay too many of them lately)... but I gotta say... I am getting tired of unpainted minis and don't really see having time to paint them any time soon, so that may turn me off from the whole thing for a bit</p>",
